{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.omega_ne_zero_imp_chiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.omega_ne_zero_imp_chiral","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.lean#L114-L122","doc":"**A nonzero bar-odd datum forces a chiral knot.**  Contrapositive of\n`omega_of_iotaFixed`: if `ω(β,p,q) ≠ 0` then the triple is *not* ι-fixed — the\nmodulus is not self-dual or the off-diagonal products differ.  This is the\nstructural reason the bar-odd `c₃` frontier required the chiral `5₂` and could\nnot be sourced from the amphichiral `4₁` (`V(4₁)_odd = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.omega_zero_on_iotaFixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.omega_zero_on_iotaFixed","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.lean#L98-L112","doc":"**Parity route to the same fact.**  On any ι-fixed triple, ι-oddness forces\n`ω = -ω`, hence `2ω = 0`, hence `ω = 0`.  Stated via the fixed-point hypotheses\n`β⁻¹ = β` (self-dual modulus) and `q = p` so that `ι(β,p,q) = (β,p,q)`; needs\nonly `2 ≠ 0` in `F`.  Mirrors the physics: an amphichiral (ι-fixed) datum has no\nbar-odd part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.omega_of_iotaFixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.omega_of_iotaFixed","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.lean#L86-L96","doc":"**Direct vanishing on the ι-fixed locus.**  If the modulus is self-dual\n(`β² = 1`, i.e. `β⁻¹ = β`) and the two off-diagonal products agree (`p = q`),\nthe bar-odd contraction is `0`.  This is the amphichiral / symmetric-search\nlocus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.sEven_iota_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.sEven_iota_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.lean#L78-L84","doc":"**The companion `s` is ι-even.**  In contrast to `ω`, the bar-even index\nshape is invariant under `ι` — so it can only ever produce ι-fixed values. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.omega_iota_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.omega_iota_odd","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.lean#L69-L76","doc":"**`ω` is ι-odd.**  The amphichiral involution `ι : (β,p,q) ↦ (β⁻¹,q,p)`\n(swap the off-diagonal products, invert the modulus) sends `ω` to `-ω`.  This is\nthe algebraic bar-oddness of the chirality channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.sEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.sEven","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.lean#L64-L67","doc":"The ι-even companion — the bar-even *index* channel shape.  Symmetric under\nthe amphichiral involution (see `sEven_iota_invariant`); this is the grade the\nsymmetric GK bilinear (B1.2) and the span-vector search (B1.3) live in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.omega","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.omega","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddAntisymOffDiagonal.lean#L58-L62","doc":"The β-graded antisymmetric off-diagonal contraction — the bar-odd channel of\nthe frame-reduced `5₂` state integral (A1 chirality split, `Im Ẑ` up to the\n`-R^{1/8}/2` chirality dressing).  `p = H⁺₂H⁻₀`, `q = H⁺₀H⁻₂`, `β` the cusp\nmodulus. ","signatureChunk":0}]}